residual 13 exact_finite_decision type audit (2026-08-24)

Method
  This audit corrects the population omission in hygiene-audit-20260815.log.
  Each contract was read in the fixed order: Lean binders and full proposition,
  Julia signature and return, quantified finite coverage, candidate/proof trust
  boundary, then independent sensitivity evidence. The manifest description was
  treated as an audit target, not controlling evidence. No checker, fixture,
  classification, registry, tolerance, formal declaration, commit, or push was
  changed by this audit.

Decision summary
  Retain exact_finite_decision: 10.
  Challenge exact_finite_decision under the current implementation: 3.
  The checker-strengthening termination condition is not yet satisfied because
  the three challenged rows still carry exact labels pending user-approved
  remediation.

RETAIN EXACT

1. adjunction.rigidity -- ACCEPT exact, with a documentation correction.
   Lean Adj.rigidity_of_gc takes alphaRel and sigmaRel plus a GaloisConnection
   proof and concludes unique alpha images plus converse membership for every
   m,e. Julia check_relational_rigidity recomputes the Galois connection for
   every subset of the complete finite M/E carriers, then exhausts every m and
   m,e conclusion. Relation callables are candidate relation data, not proof
   oracles. Exactness is conditional on duplicate-free complete carriers and
   relation images remaining inside them; the current manifest should state
   those conditions explicitly.

2. viability.closure_object -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean viabilityClosureImage_left_fixed unfolds to reflexive successor closure
   of viableSet equalling viableSet for a ViableSystem. Julia enumerates every
   source/target pair on the supplied complete carrier, independently recomputes
   step_closed, successor closure, and equality. step and viable are object data;
   the ViableSystem proof is not accepted as Bool.

3. viability.relational_frame -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean viabilityRelationalFrame_left_fixed fixes pi to identityRel, rho to
   reflexiveStepRel, and kappa to viableSet. Julia constructs those relations,
   reuses finite Phi/successor closure, recomputes step_closed, and compares the
   full finite image with viableSet. No proof field is supplied.

4. layers.viable_to_hilbert -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean viableToHilbert_nontrivial_iff states WldNontrivial of the canonical
   one-dimensional composite iff viableSet is inhabited. Julia first validates
   the finite ViableSystem premise, constructs the relational frame and hinge,
   constructs the zero-or-identity 1x1 loop, and compares nontriviality with
   viable-set nonemptiness. The loop is computed rather than supplied.

5. bridge.hinge_object_classifier -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean hingeClassifyingLoop_nontrivial_iff uses the complete hinge relations and
   their selected kappa/epsilon images. Julia recomputes Act, constructs the
   canonical zero-or-identity loop, validates an independent 1x1 candidate
   against it, and decides nontriviality iff hinge nonemptiness. Finite relation
   images are the full data relevant to the existential; no proof Bool is used.

6. bridge.hinge_lax_map -- ACCEPT exact, with a stale-assumption correction.
   Lean hingeClassifyingLoop_lax assumes HingeForward and concludes the norm
   inequality for the zero-or-identity classifiers. The additive Julia method
   does not receive a forward-preservation Bool: it recomputes both Act
   nonemptiness values, forward implication, both candidate/canonical loop
   equalities, and the 1D norm inequality. The manifest sentence claiming a
   supplied forward Boolean is stale and must be removed.

7. bridge.hinge_thin_functor -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean hingeClassifierFunctor_nontrivial_iff reduces the functor object to the
   same canonical hinge classifier. The additive Julia method uses the shared
   independent-candidate checker, which recomputes hinge nonemptiness and the
   zero-or-identity loop before deciding the iff.

8. bridge.hinge_hilbert_functor -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean strictHingeHilbertFunctor_nontrivial_iff is an object theorem and has no
   arrow premise. The additive Julia method recomputes the complete hinge
   classifier and validates the supplied 1x1 loop before deciding the same
   nontriviality iff. It does not use the legacy three-Bool functor-law method.

9. bridge.hinge_structural_functor -- ACCEPT exact.
   Lean StructuralHingeData contains only a CompleteHingeData object; structural
   isomorphisms are morphisms, not additional object fields. The object theorem
   reduces to the strict classifier iff. Julia's additive method validates the
   supplied structural object loop against the complete hinge datum and decides
   the same equivalence.

10. graded.presheaf_transition_output_copair_unique -- ACCEPT exact.
    Lean quantifies every tag and every y in the target fiber, assumes component
    agreement, and concludes extensional equality with the Sigma copair. Julia
    validates the finite presheaf/coproduct data, enumerates every transition tag
    and every value in the complete target fiber, recomputes component agreement,
    and exhausts the same candidate equality. handlers and candidate are map
    data, not proof flags.

CHALLENGE CURRENT EXACT LABEL

11. viability.closure_functor -- REJECT exact until Equiv validation is fixed.
    Lean viabilityClosureFunctor_left_natural receives f whose mapConfig is an
    Equiv. The additive Julia method calls a mapping "bijective" when its key set
    equals the source carrier and its value set equals the target carrier, but it
    never checks injectivity or equal cardinality. Concrete counterexample:
      source=[:a,:b,:c], target=[:x,:y],
      mapping=Dict(:a=>:x,:b=>:x,:c=>:y), no steps, no viable states,
      source_subsets=powerset(source).
    The checker returns bijective=true and contract_holds=true for this non-Equiv.
    Minimal remediation: validate duplicate-free carriers, totality, injectivity,
    surjectivity, and inverse round trips before the naturality equation. Re-audit
    exact after that change. Without remediation, complete_only is the strongest
    justified direction under an explicit faithful-Equiv assumption.

12. bridge.hinge_strict_functor -- REJECT exact; proof premise is self-reported.
    Lean strictHingeClassifier_identity_intertwines receives h : X <= Y, i.e. an
    equivalence of source and target hinge truth. The additive Julia method takes
    only two arbitrary 0/1 matrices plus arrow_valid::Bool. It neither receives
    the two CompleteHingeData values nor independently recomputes h; it conjoins
    the supplied Boolean with loop equality and intertwining. Repackaging a Lean
    premise as a Boolean is explicitly excluded by the shared exact rule.
    Minimal remediation: accept complete finite source/target hinge data,
    recompute both canonical loops and the truth equivalence, then test identity
    intertwining. Until then, complete_only is justified only under explicit
    faithful-arrow and canonical-loop assumptions.

13. reference_models.v5_1 -- REJECT exact under the declared scope.
    Lean RefModel.reference_models is the closed conjunction of three next
    equations on RefState.s0/s1/s2. The Julia v5_1 projection checks the complete
    literal carrier and all three equations, which is the correct core. However,
    check_reference_models(candidate) first requires fields for three unrelated
    stable/dynamic/nondegenerate contracts. A candidate containing exactly the
    complete three-state carrier and next map in the manifest scope is rejected
    before v5_1_contract_holds is evaluated. Thus the checker has false negatives
    caused by unrelated fields and is not an exact decision of this target.
    Minimal remediation: add a dedicated closed v5.1 decoder/checker accepting
    only states and next (or split validation before dispatch), reject unknown and
    missing v5 fields, and retain the literal three-equation oracle. Until then,
    regression_only is the safe fixed-object classification.

Sensitivity evidence
  All 13 rows have registry entries, but registry membership does not repair the
  three semantic gaps. The strict negative mutates a target loop while keeping
  arrow_valid=true and never tests the proof source. The closure-functor fixture
  uses equal-size bijective carriers and misses the noninjective case. The v5.1
  fixture supplies every unrelated model field and therefore misses the
  overconstraint. These are coverage gaps, not reasons to weaken existing tests.

Required next decision
  The user must choose whether to remediate the three checkers and retain exact,
  or downgrade their classifications and remove them from the exact sensitivity
  registry. No classification or registry mutation is authorized by this
  read-only stage.
